# Supabase (must match the backend / JWT for the API environment you use)
# Supabase (must match the backend / JWT for the API environment you use)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- API target: same rule for user, subscription, payments, trades ---
# Set VITE_APP_ENV to: prod | dev | local
# - prod → https://api.tradeguardx.com/{user|subscription|payments|trades}
# - dev  → https://dev.api.tradeguardx.com/...
# - local → localhost ports (3000 user, 3001 subscription, 3002 payments, 3009 trades)
# If VITE_APP_ENV is omitted, defaults to prod.
VITE_APP_ENV=prod

# Optional: override ONE service only (full base including path segment, no trailing slash)
# Example — payments only to dev while rest stay on prod (unusual; prefer one VITE_APP_ENV):
# VITE_PAYMENTS_API_BASE_URL=https://dev.api.tradeguardx.com/payments
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tradeguardx.com/user
# VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tradeguardx.com/subscription
# VITE_TRADE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tradeguardx.com/trades

# --- API target: same rule for user, subscription, payments, trades ---
# Set VITE_APP_ENV to: prod | dev | local
# - prod → https://api.tradeguardx.com/{user|subscription|payments|trades}
# - dev  → https://dev.api.tradeguardx.com/...
# - local → localhost ports (3000 user, 3001 subscription, 3002 payments, 3009 trades)
# If VITE_APP_ENV is omitted, defaults to prod.
VITE_APP_ENV=prod

# Optional: override ONE service only (full base including path segment, no trailing slash)
# Example — payments only to dev while rest stay on prod (unusual; prefer one VITE_APP_ENV):
# VITE_PAYMENTS_API_BASE_URL=https://dev.api.tradeguardx.com/payments
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tradeguardx.com/user
# VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tradeguardx.com/subscription
# VITE_TRADE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tradeguardx.com/trades

# Beta registration at /beta-traders — POST to Formspree (or similar). Required for form submit button.
# VITE_BETA_SIGNUP_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/your-form-id

# --- Sentry error tracking (optional) ---
# When VITE_SENTRY_DSN is unset, Sentry init is a no-op and nothing is reported.
# Create a project at https://sentry.io → settings → projects → "tradeguardx-web"
# → Client Keys (DSN) and paste it here. The release tag below buckets errors
# per deploy (set to your CI commit SHA or version string in production).
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://abc123@o0.ingest.sentry.io/000000
# VITE_APP_VERSION=0.0.1

# --- Top-of-page promo strip (src/components/promo/ActivePromo.jsx) ---
# TWO MODES, and FOUNDING-MEMBER WINS when both are configured. To show the
# discount banner you must set VITE_FOUNDING_MEMBER_ACTIVE=false, or nothing
# changes — only one strip fits at the top of the viewport.
#
# Mode 1 — founding member. The grant is the free trial itself, so
# VITE_FOUNDING_MEMBER_TRIAL_DAYS MUST MATCH the backend's TRIAL_DAYS
# (subscription-service + user-service serverless.yml). Nothing enforces this;
# when they disagree the site promises access that signup does not deliver.
# VITE_FOUNDING_MEMBER_ACTIVE=true
# VITE_FOUNDING_MEMBER_LIMIT=100
# VITE_FOUNDING_MEMBER_TRIAL_DAYS=7
# VITE_FOUNDING_MEMBER_PLAN=Pro+
#
# Mode 2 — discount code, with a live countdown. Renders
# "<DISCOUNT>% off all paid plans" plus a copyable code.
#
# THE CODE MUST EXIST AS A DISCOUNT IN DODO FIRST. Dodo SILENTLY IGNORES an
# unknown code — no error, no warning — so advertising a code that was never
# created means customers are charged full price believing they got the
# discount. Create it in the Dodo dashboard (or via
# payments-service/src/dodo/dodoDiscounts.ts) before setting these.
#
# The pricing page sends this code automatically at checkout; an influencer
# `?ref=` code takes precedence when both are present.
# VITE_ACTIVE_PROMO_CYCLES MUST MATCH the Dodo discount's subscription_cycles.
# It only changes wording ("50% off your first month" vs "off all paid plans"),
# but getting it wrong advertises an ongoing price you never actually charge.
# VITE_ACTIVE_PROMO_CODE=LAUNCH50
# VITE_ACTIVE_PROMO_DISCOUNT=50
# VITE_ACTIVE_PROMO_CYCLES=1
# VITE_ACTIVE_PROMO_EXPIRES_AT=2026-09-30T23:59:59Z
# The eyebrow above the headline — the framing line, e.g. "EARLY BIRD OFFER".
# The headline itself is derived from DISCOUNT + CYCLES, not written here.
# VITE_ACTIVE_PROMO_HEADLINE=LAUNCH SPECIAL
#
# Create the matching coupon first:
#   cd tradeguardx-payments-service
#   npm run create-promo -- --code LAUNCH50 --pct 50 --cycles 1 --limit 100
